From: Gee <gehee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ubi: zero a NAND eraseblock's header pages before erasing it

The stock Caddx Ascent Lite/Lite+ kernel zeroes the first two minimal I/O units of
a NAND eraseblock (the EC and VID headers) before erasing it, so that a block
whose erasure was cut short by a power loss cannot keep valid-looking old
headers. HiSilicon's SDK kernel, which fpvOS builds, lacks this.

Reconstructed from the stock kernel's ubi_io_sync_erase(): the same call
sequence (__vmalloc, memset, mtd_write, vfree), sizes, flags (GFP_NOFS) and
messages, in the same place, the !nor_flash branch next to
nor_erase_prepare(). The stock source is not available.
---
--- a/drivers/mtd/ubi/io.c	2026-10-03 23:25:38.500153532 -0400
+++ b/drivers/mtd/ubi/io.c	2026-10-03 23:25:38.510363279 -0400
@@ -76,6 +76,7 @@
 #include <linux/crc32.h>
 #include <linux/err.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
+#include <linux/vmalloc.h>
 #include "ubi.h"
 
 static int self_check_not_bad(const struct ubi_device *ubi, int pnum);
@@ -505,6 +506,39 @@
 }
 
 /**
+ * nand_erase_prepare - prepare a NAND flash physical eraseblock for erasure.
+ * @ubi: UBI device description object
+ * @pnum: physical eraseblock number to prepare
+ *
+ * Zero the first two minimal I/O units of the eraseblock, where the EC and
+ * VID headers live, before it is erased. If power is cut while the erasure is
+ * in progress, the old headers then fail their checks at the next attach,
+ * instead of possibly surviving on a half-erased block. This is the NAND
+ * counterpart of nor_erase_prepare(). Failure is only reported: the erasure
+ * goes ahead either way.
+ *
+ * Recovered from the stock Caddx Ascent Lite/Lite+ kernel (5.10.221, built
+ * 2026-08-14), which does this; HiSilicon's SDK 1.0.2.0 kernel does not.
+ */
+static void nand_erase_prepare(struct ubi_device *ubi, int pnum)
+{
+	int len = 2 * ubi->min_io_size;
+	loff_t addr = (loff_t)pnum * ubi->peb_size;
+	size_t written;
+	void *buf;
+
+	buf = __vmalloc(len, GFP_NOFS);
+	if (!buf) {
+		ubi_err(ubi, "cannot allocate memory to nand_erase_prepare");
+		return;
+	}
+	memset(buf, 0, len);
+	if (mtd_write(ubi->mtd, addr, len, &written, buf))
+		ubi_err(ubi, "nand_erase_prepare write err");
+	vfree(buf);
+}
+
+/**
  * ubi_io_sync_erase - synchronously erase a physical eraseblock.
  * @ubi: UBI device description object
  * @pnum: physical eraseblock number to erase
@@ -539,6 +573,8 @@
 		err = nor_erase_prepare(ubi, pnum);
 		if (err)
 			return err;
+	} else {
+		nand_erase_prepare(ubi, pnum);
 	}
 
 	if (torture) {
